1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Naka River,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoes flew off too.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
Onto the head of a carpenter I was chopping,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow summon
some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
pachinko, saving up,
a yawn or two, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streets feel strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's water flask,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset sinks toward the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this too,
won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,700
In Katsushika Shibamata,
they say happiness is here too.

12
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:22,440
Only after losing it did I realize.

13
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:24,520
Because I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:58,980
Food.

15
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:02,580
Food.

16
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,640
Ryo-san!

17
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,940
Thanks for the meal.

18
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:16,720
Saved!

19
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,780
I had no money and hadn't
eaten anything for three days.

20
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,820
With a Ryo-san like this around,

21
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:25,800
I can't leave the place unattended.

22
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,140
Are you going somewhere?

23
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:30,060
Even I want to take a
day off once in a while

24
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:32,260
and go to a hot spring or something.

25
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:35,200
But you see, if someone hungry

26
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,980
came around in the middle of
the night to ransack the kitchen,

27
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:40,680
I'd be too worried to go anywhere.

28
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:42,740
No, Grandma.

29
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,640
Tomorrow's my day off,

30
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:47,000
so I'll be fine for a while too.

31
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:49,960
Go to a hot spring or wherever you like.

32
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:51,720
Really?

33
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:53,060
Yeah, I'm fine.

34
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:57,240
I'm not going to take away an
old person's little pleasures.

35
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,540
Is that so?

36
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:02,240
No, actually, there's a cheap trip
through the neighborhood association.

37
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:05,980
If Ryo-san says it's okay, I think I'll go.

38
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:08,120
Go on, go on.

39
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:10,300
Well, I'll leave this with you.

40
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:10,760
What's this?

41
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:12,300
It's for travel expenses.

42
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:14,480
Travel expenses?

43
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:18,280
If anything comes up,
manage with that money, okay?

44
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:19,640
Got it.

45
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:24,760
Auntie, leave Ryo to me
and go enjoy the hot springs.

46
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,440
What is this?

47
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:34,280
Today and tomorrow,
Community Affairs' Ryotsu-sensei will

48
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:37,280
be filling in for Yone-san,

49
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:40,760
so behave yourselves and
don't cause any trouble. -Ryotsu

50
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,860
If Ryotsu is Yone-san,

51
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:48,320
I guess. The top pick is Misawa Prince,
and second is Tsurutarō.

52
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:52,320
Damn it, we've been totally wiped out!

53
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:57,240
Dammit, dammit, dammit! But with this,
the money Auntie entrusted to us

54
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:01,400
is completely gone. We've got to do something,
or we're in trouble.

55
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:06,940
Hey, Ryotsu! What's going on with you two?

56
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:12,160
The washing machine stopped working.
The washing machine?

57
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,440
It's not going to work at all,
is it, Ryotsu?

58
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,920
Of course it won't work
if you cram it this full.

59
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:24,020
Just pull some of the laundry out.

60
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,000
Yone-san, I'm counting on you.

61
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:29,200
Didn't it say not to cause any trouble?

62
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:31,600
Ugh, this is such a pain.

63
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:39,060
Even the damn screw came off.

64
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,600
Senpai, what are we supposed to do?

65
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,520
Then it's just a box now

66
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:43,880
Yeah.

67
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,780
Do something about it, Ryo-san.

68
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,200
That's right,
it's your responsibility, after all.

69
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,560
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

70
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:53,800
I'll take it to the dry cleaner's for you.

71
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:55,240
Really?

72
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:57,740
Yeah, bring over all the laundry.

73
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:58,640
No, whites.

74
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:00,100
Much appreciated.

75
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,060
Much appreciated.

76
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:06,800
Why on earth do I have to

77
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:09,680
Isn't this supposed to be the senior's job?

78
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,500
Because you're Ryo-bo, after all.

79
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,700
Shouldn't we help each
other when we're in trouble?

80
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:17,920
You only say that when
you're the one in trouble.

81
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:18,920
Did you say something?

82
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:21,280
Is the dry cleaner's still not finished?

83
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,500
A coin laundry? Seriously?

84
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,340
So it's 200 yen a load?

85
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:27,680
Hold on.

86
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:31,200
If the cleaning costs
are 2,000 yen per person,

87
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,040
then using a coin laundry

88
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:37,440
Honda! We're washing here!

89
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:41,160
Senpai, this is a coin laundry, isn't it!

90
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:44,520
I know that.
We just have to wash the load, right?

91
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:46,600
Come on, put everyone's clothes in.

92
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:48,940
Mine too, while you're at it.

93
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:49,980
Senpai.

94
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:56,060
You take yours off too. If we wash them all together,
we'll save on the washing fees.

95
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,060
No, no.

96
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:01,980
Who cares, we won't get caught.

97
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:03,640
Senpai, that's cruel.

98
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:14,080
Ha ha ha ha

99
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:18,220
What's wrong? Calm down, Honda.

100
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:20,980
But senpai, if someone comes,

101
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:24,920
no one would come out in this downpour.

102
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:26,560
Aaaaah!

103
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:27,800
What happened?

104
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:29,300
I-it's Reiko!

105
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:34,980
I'll have to rewash the
sheets I hung out to dry.

106
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:38,000
Of all people, Reiko had to show up.

107
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,240
What should we do, senpai?

108
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:42,100
We hide!

109
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:43,980
Hide where?

110
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,220
Where, you ask?

111
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:48,140
The ceiling!

112
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:50,760
Just hurry up!

113
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:51,680
Okay.

114
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:02,880
Hurry up and go, Honda.

115
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:08,060
It's no use. I'm going up first.

116
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,400
Come on.

117
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:31,800
W-what a super pervert!

118
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:33,640
Nooooo!

119
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:35,600
I don't want to know anymore!

120
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,520
Not at all, yes.

121
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:41,920
R-Reiko didn't hold back, did she?

122
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,500
Yo!

123
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:54,360
Did this Rei run away?

124
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:59,080
Honestly, what a national disgrace you are,

125
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:03,520
so this is what Reiko-kun asked us to bring.

126
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,180
We were supposed to dry
it in the dryer, right.

127
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:08,300
Now the Chief is coming,

128
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,800
meddling

129
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,820
If they notice us,

130
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:12,940
Shall we do it here?

131
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:13,540
No.

132
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:22,900
Thirty minutes of drying should be enough.

133
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:49,260
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

134
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:53,620
Honda, what are you doing, you idiot?

135
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,260
Looks like it got sunburned, though

136
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:02,840
It's a miracle it's still alive.

137
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:06,540
Well, all that's left is pressing it.

138
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:10,260
Let's have them do it here.

139
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:16,220
Ryo-san, you're a rare sight.
What brings you here?

140
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,920
I've got a favor to ask of the boss.

141
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:20,460
Pressing the laundry?

142
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:23,620
Our factory doesn't
really do that kind of -

143
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:24,580
Just make it rough, that's fine.

144
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:26,260
As long as the wrinkles come out.

145
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:31,140
Hey! The cleaning's done!

146
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:34,120
Ryotsu, what is this?

147
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,720
It's stiff as tin!

148
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:39,660
I used plenty of starch and pressed it, so.

149
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:42,260
My body's so stiff I can't move.

150
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:44,000
These hurt too much to wear.

151
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:45,960
You're charging 2,000 yen for this?

152
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:48,120
Shut up! Don't be so picky!

153
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:52,760
It was Honda clogging the washing machine
that caused this in the first place, right?

154
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,840
It was Ryotsu who broke the washing machine!

155
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,220
Sorry, Ryo-san.

156
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:02,460
I slipped in the bathroom, you see.

157
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:04,900
You can't come home for a while?

158
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:07,600
So that means...

159
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:10,560
It means Ryotsu will be
the dorm matron for a while.

160
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:12,080
I don't want that.

161
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:13,440
What did you say?!

162
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:21,201
So, until Auntie comes back, we

163
00:10:21,251 --> 00:10:24,700
will have to get by on Ryotsu's cunning.

164
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:26,980
But why is Ryotsu the one who...?

165
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:31,860
No, forget the unnecessary policies!
Think more positively!

166
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:33,380
That's unreasonable.

167
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,605
That's why I have a brilliant idea.

168
00:10:35,655 --> 00:10:38,600
I really want everyone to cooperate on this.

169
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:39,480
A brilliant idea?

170
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:40,620
What is it?

171
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:44,920
What?! Rent out the empty rooms?!

172
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:48,580
Seven rooms are sitting empty.
There's no reason to let them go to waste.

173
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:51,820
We're in trouble if the administrative
officer finds out, Senpai.

174
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:55,020
That's why I'm telling you to
cooperate so he doesn't find out.

175
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:56,040
Excuse me.

176
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:58,360
Right away, a prospective tenant!

177
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:00,620
Hello.

178
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,760
You're 21?

179
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:07,320
Nice to meet you.

180
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:12,680
I'm starting to think the senior
officers aren't so bad after all.

181
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:14,900
I think so too.

182
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:17,120
Now, we'll move on to the screening.

183
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:18,880
Yes, you've passed.

184
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,480
Super lucky!

185
00:11:21,460 --> 00:11:23,540
You're approved, apparently.

186
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:26,520
Thank you,
I look forward to working with you.

187
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:27,900
Welcome aboard.

188
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:30,540
