247
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,920
I mean, like I said...

248
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:28,500
Honda.

249
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,940
What is it, senpai?

250
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,540
This guy's just too quiet.

251
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:37,420
I figured I'd just give him something to hold,
you know, Honda.

252
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:38,920
Come on, Honda, why don't you try riding it?

253
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:42,060
Why a tricycle, of all things?

254
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:47,120
I'm the Honda of this kind, you know.

255
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:48,880
Try dancing.

256
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:52,800
So anything with handlebars will do?

257
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:54,180
One, two.

258
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:56,120
One, two.

259
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:57,780
One, two.

260
00:14:57,780 --> 00:14:58,600
One, two.

261
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,600
One, two.

262
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,540
Let's go

263
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:01,440
Let's go

264
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,820
Let's go dancing

265
00:15:02,820 --> 00:15:04,140
Let's go

266
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:07,040
Ryotsu,
don't tell me you have a woman up there?

267
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,660
Of course not, what are you talking about?

268
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:10,740
Then what's this voice?

269
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:11,820
Well, this is

270
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:13,480
You're hiding something, aren't you?

271
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,580
Hiding? Whatever gave you that idea?

272
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,780
It's this room, isn't it?

273
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:17,220
Open up, Ryotsu!

274
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:18,000
Well

275
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:20,100
Move aside, I'll open it myself!

276
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:21,580
No, you can't, Chief!

277
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:22,740
Why not?

278
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:23,560
Because it's the decent thing to do.

279
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:25,880
What nonsense are you babbling about?

280
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:46,780
Looks like we managed to fool him somehow.

281
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:50,400
That guy.

282
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:54,980
Does Sakonji always dress like
that and do that sort of thing?

283
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:56,820
All the time.

284
00:15:56,820 --> 00:15:59,540
What on earth is he thinking?

285
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:00,540
Look, Ken-chan.

286
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:04,260
Just give Mom's bra back already.

287
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:05,560
What is this?

288
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:08,880
It's obviously the TV, Chief.

289
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:10,660
Something seems fishy.

290
00:16:10,660 --> 00:16:13,100
What are you talking about?
It's the TV, I tell you, the TV!

291
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:17,780
Well then, Chief, enjoy yourself in
this room tonight, all by yourself.

292
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:28,480
We've got to keep the Chief
locked in a room tonight somehow,

293
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:31,360
or he'll find out we've been
renting the rooms without permission.

294
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,840
But how?

295
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:35,680
That's what I'm trying to figure out,
isn't it!

296
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:37,140
Mr. Otani.

297
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:39,120
Is the bath free?

298
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:42,900
Yes, it's free, it's free,
go ahead, go ahead!

299
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:45,120
It's to the right at the end of the hall.

300
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,520
Okay.

301
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:50,460
If the Chief finds us,
we're completely done for.

302
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:53,260
That's why I'm thinking about what to do,
isn't it!

303
00:16:54,060 --> 00:16:54,580
That's it!

304
00:16:56,320 --> 00:17:00,040
I hear the chief has been
really into poetry lately.

305
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:00,800
That's it!

306
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,340
What do you mean, "that's it"?

307
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:05,320
Chief, what's wrong?

308
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:07,400
I was thinking of taking a bath.

309
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:09,900
Senpai, this is bad.

310
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:10,500
Just understand.

311
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:13,640
Chief, I actually have a favor to ask.

312
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,580
What's this all of a sudden?

313
00:17:15,580 --> 00:17:18,920
Since you're staying at the
Nikoniko Dormitory tonight, Chief,

314
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:23,220
we'd really love to hear
one of your signature poems.

315
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:26,000
You want to hear my poetry?

316
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,640
Please, we're begging you.

317
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:30,620
Even at Katsushika Police Station,
you're quite famous.

318
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:33,460
My poetry is that well known?

319
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:35,240
It's already a huge hit.

320
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:38,960
Please, please,
let us hear the Chief's poetry too.

321
00:17:39,380 --> 00:17:42,020
Well, if you're going to insist that much,
I suppose I have no choice.

322
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:43,720
Thank you in advance.

323
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:44,940
Fine.

324
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:52,110
About the Chief's famous poetry recital...

325
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:55,580
It's famous, all right,
but only for being terrible.

326
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:58,540
At the banquet the other day,

327
00:17:58,590 --> 00:18:01,120
I heard thirty people collapsed.

328
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:04,810
We can't handle this on our own.

329
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:07,640
If it's come to this,
we're taking everyone down with us!

330
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:17,120
Why do we have to go along with this too?

331
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:19,100
Because our senpai is pushy.

332
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:21,900
Even though it takes
three hours to get home.

333
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:23,780
You there!
After you die, do it by correspondence!

334
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:28,960
Now we will begin the solo recital of the dead,
by Master Ohara.

335
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,260
Master Ohara, please.

336
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:32,480
Well then.

337
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:37,080
Benmasa, shuku shuku!

338
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:41,240
What is this!
That pig has been strangled to death.

339
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:42,980
It's torture!

340
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:45,580
I had no idea it would be this bad.

341
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:51,620
What's wrong, everyone?

342
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:57,580
No, it's just that the Chief's passionate
performance got us all fired up too.

343
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:00,620
I'll open the window for a bit.

344
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:03,900
Oh no.

345
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:08,520
Keeping it shut is better for the effect,
isn't it?

346
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:11,480
Then from the beginning.

347
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:14,620
From the beginning again?

348
00:19:15,260 --> 00:19:16,480
Of course.

349
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:19,260
Getting to hear the Chief's
poetry from the very start again...

350
00:19:19,820 --> 00:19:21,340
What could be a greater happiness?

351
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:22,700
Come on, Chief.

352
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:24,980
Please, once more from the beginning.

353
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:27,660
Well then.

354
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:29,140
Benshō.

355
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,540
Chief, sorry.

356
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:35,300
I'd love to keep listening,

357
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:37,220
but it's almost the last train time.

358
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:38,620
I see.

359
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:40,400
Terai lives far away, after all.

360
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,720
Sorry.

361
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:44,500
What a real shame.

362
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:46,900
Yeah, it's a real pity, Terai.

363
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:51,240
Let's have Terai enjoy
it properly another day.

364
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:57,840
Well then, off to the toilet

365
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:01,960
I need to use the restroom for a sec.

366
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:04,560
I see. Then I'll come along too.

367
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:06,380
Chief, you can't go.

368
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:09,520
We've just gotten into the swing of things,
haven't we?

369
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:12,600
Something like that. You don't really
want to go to the toilet, do you?

370
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:16,560
Chief, if you leave this room,
it's all over for us!

371
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:17,220
Yes.

372
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:19,540
There's something going on here,
isn't there.

373
00:20:19,540 --> 00:20:22,140
You don't need to put up
with this and play along.

374
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:23,420
Looks that way.

375
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,660
Sorry, Chief.

376
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:27,840
Tonight, Dad's coming up from Kobe,

377
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:30,740
so I have to go pick
him up at Tokyo Station.

378
00:20:30,740 --> 00:20:33,020
Sorry, I also need to...

379
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:36,800
Everyone seems busy, but

380
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:39,080
shall we call it a night here?

381
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:39,740
What?

382
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:42,000
No, Chief, that's not it.

383
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,840
We really want to hear more, nice and slow.

384
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:46,760
Whaaat!

385
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:50,860
You're cornered!
There's nowhere for you to run!

386
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:53,460
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

387
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:54,289
N-no, it's nothing.

388
00:20:54,339 --> 00:20:57,680
Your shigin moved me so
much I started crying, Chief.

389
00:20:58,320 --> 00:21:01,120
I see. Then let's really go all out!

390
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:03,200
Hey! Chief, you're the best in all of Japan!

391
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:04,480
Mm-hmm.

392
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:09,480
Banzai!

393
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:10,920
Ooh!

394
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:13,860
Here we go!

395
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:14,980
Whoa!

396
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,440
Whoa!

397
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:20,620
Rats are running everywhere!

398
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:23,620
Idiot!

399
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:26,760
When did the cockroaches
start running away too?

400
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:28,800
Senpei's!

401
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,940
Whoa!

402
00:21:32,060 --> 00:21:33,500
The crabs!

403
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:35,220
Whoa!

404
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:36,940
Whoa!

405
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:41,960
What is this?!

406
00:22:01,620 --> 00:22:03,180
It's no use!

407
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:05,320
Migaku! You guys!

408
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:09,320
Right, if we just pass out,
we'll be free of this.

409
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:10,960
Come on, Nakagawa!

410
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:12,100
Me too.

411
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:13,340
Sagonji, you too!

412
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:15,660
He's really getting into it!

413
00:22:17,060 --> 00:22:17,820
Quick battle!

414
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:20,360
Resistance battle!

415
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:38,680


416
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:39,980
Aaaaaaaaaa

417
00:22:39,980 --> 00:22:40,900
Aaaaaaaaaa

418
00:22:40,900 --> 00:22:41,920
Aaaaaaaaaa

419
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:43,520
Aaaaaaaaaa

420
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:44,760
Aaaaaaaaaa

421
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:12,540
Aaaaaaaah!

422
00:23:12,540 --> 00:23:13,060
Aaaaaaaah!

423
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:14,460
Aaaaaaaah!

424
00:23:14,460 --> 00:23:16,440
Aaaaaaaah!

425
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:16,540
Aaaaaaaah!

426
00:23:16,540 --> 00:23:17,720
Aaaaaaaah!

427
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:19,980
Aaaaaaaah!

428
00:23:19,980 --> 00:23:20,360
Aaaaaaaah!

429
00:23:20,360 --> 00:23:20,980
Aaaaaaaah!

430
00:23:20,980 --> 00:23:26,500
Aaaaaaaah!

431
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:33,020
What on earth happened here?

432
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,700
Looks like we at least
escaped with our lives.

433
00:23:37,700 --> 00:23:38,940
Hey, Chief Ohara.

434
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:41,200
I'm moving out of this dump!

435
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:42,960
Yeah, this is too much!

436
00:23:42,960 --> 00:23:45,080
Please return our deposit and key money.

437
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,220
Well

438
00:23:46,220 --> 00:23:47,240
Ryotsu!

439
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:49,760
So that's what it was.

440
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:52,500
Well, there are various reasons for this...

441
00:23:52,500 --> 00:23:56,020
You rented out the police dormitory without permission,
didn't you?

442
00:23:56,500 --> 00:23:57,780
BAKAMOON!

443
00:23:58,340 --> 00:24:00,120
Sure enough, it ends like this!

444
00:24:05,740 --> 00:24:08,140
Chief! Is it true you have a mistress?

445
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,780
And a secret child on top of that?

446
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,480
How enviable!

447
00:24:11,500 --> 00:24:12,700
No, no, how terrifying!

448
00:24:13,140 --> 00:24:14,740
Your wife and Hiromi will cry!

449
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:17,360
Chief! Aren't you even ashamed of yourself?

450
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:18,140
As a human being!

451
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:20,700
Wrong! The chief's secret child scandal!

452
00:24:20,980 --> 00:24:21,560
Nice to meet you!

453
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:37,220
They say I'm a woman who can't fall in love,

454
00:24:37,220 --> 00:24:42,900
but I have mountains of things I want to do.

455
00:24:44,800 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride my motorbike
across the vast desert.

456
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,120
I want to be freer than a bird.

457
00:25:00,020 --> 00:25:07,140
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

458
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:15,280
Sorry, my heart, please wait for me.

459
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:22,200
Panoramic future,
the dazzle comes so quickly.

460
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:26,526
You understand, right?

461
00:25:26,576 --> 00:25:30,060
Sorry, please wait for me.

